<title>ECUADOR: Ecuador net reserves rise to $2.05 bln in April.</title>
<headline>Ecuador net reserves rise to $2.05 bln in April.</headline>
<dateline>QUITO 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ecuador's Central Bank said Tuesday its net international reserves grew 6.6 percent or $128 million to $2.05 billion in April.</p>
<p>In April 1996, international reserves stood at $1.59 billion.</p>
<p>The Central Bank explained that the increase in reserves was due to major oil exports and dollar purchases.</p>
<p>Reserves stood at $1.832 billion at the end of last year, up $276 million from the end of 1995.</p>
<p>((-- Gustavo Oviedo, Quito Newsroom, 5932 258433))</p>
